From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:08:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: wake the queue on remote completions, except for
 threaded drivers

190bdeee disabled the wake-up of the IO thread of a queue when a request
completes on another thread, as it doubled the wake-ups with qcow2, which
returns the responses itself with tapdisk_vbd_kick(). But the completions of
the NBD client, on the main thread, then no longer wake the queue: during a
storage migration, the responses of the mirrored writes wait until something
else wakes the queue, the guest can't freeze its tasks to suspend, and the
migration fails ("freeze kernel threads failed -16" in the guest, emu-manager
"Failed to read from xenopsd because timeout reached").

Wake the queue again, except when the request completes in a threaded
driver, and make qcow2 also kick the queue for a failed request.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/block-qcow2.c |  3 ++-
 drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c | 11 ++++++++---
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block-qcow2.c b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
index 4d43a0ce..633c788d 100644
--- a/drivers/block-qcow2.c
+++ b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
@@ -722,7 +722,8 @@ signal_completion(struct qcow2_request *r)
 	notify = td_complete_request(r->treq, r->error);
 	DBG(TLOG_DBG, "lsec: 0x%08"PRIx64", blk: 0x%04x, "
 		"err: %d\n", r->treq.sec, r->treq.secs, r->error);
-	if (r->error == 0 && notify) {
+	/* Also on error: the generic wake-up of remote completions skips qcow2 */
+	if (notify) {
 		tapdisk_vbd_kick(queue, true);
 		s->kick++;
 	}
diff --git a/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c b/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
index 38e2313c..59662371 100644
--- a/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
+++ b/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
@@ -1585,11 +1585,14 @@ __tapdisk_vbd_complete_td_request(td_vbd_queue_t* queue, td_vbd_request_t *vreq,
 	 * completed by the NBD client on the main thread), wake it up:
 	 * otherwise the response waits until something else wakes it up, which
 	 * may never happen if the guest stopped sending requests (e.g. while
-	 * suspending for a live migration).
+	 * suspending for a live migration). Threaded drivers (qcow2) return the
+	 * responses themselves with tapdisk_vbd_kick(), which wakes the IO
+	 * thread after: waking it here too makes it race with the driver thread
+	 * for queue->mutex and doubles the wake-ups.
 	 */
-	if (notify && !tapdisk_server_in_io_thread(queue - vbd->queues))
+	if (notify && !tapdisk_server_in_io_thread(queue - vbd->queues) &&
+	    !(image->driver && td_flag_test(image->driver->ops->flags, TD_DRIVER_THREADED)))
 		tapdisk_vbd_wake_queue(queue);
-
 	if (err != -EBUSY) {
 		int write = treq.op == TD_OP_WRITE;
 		// FIXME: should we take a lock here for stats ? or use an atomic ?
@@ -1791,6 +1794,8 @@ tapdisk_vbd_complete_block_status_request(td_request_t treq, int res)
 	return __tapdisk_vbd_complete_td_request(queue, vreq, treq, res);
 }
 
+/* Called by td_complete_request(), either from IO thread or another thread
+ * like with QCOW2 */
 static int
 tapdisk_vbd_complete_td_request_cb(td_request_t treq, int res)
 {
